# ── Local development ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to .env.local, fill both values in, then restart `npm run dev`
# (Vite only reads env files at startup).
#
# Both come from your Supabase dashboard: Project Settings -> API.
# The anon key is a publishable client key, safe to ship in the browser bundle —
# row-level security is what protects the data. Never put the service_role key
# here; it bypasses RLS entirely and must stay server-side.

# Hosted project (already linked from GitHub/Vercel integrations):
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://tekzjuuerbozevmznymd.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# ── Vercel production ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env.local is never uploaded. After (re)creating the Vercel project from this
# GitHub repo, set the same two names under:
#   Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables → Production
# then Redeploy. Vite inlines VITE_* at build time, so a redeploy is required
# after changing them.
#
# Also in Supabase → Authentication → URL Configuration:
#   Site URL:      https://<your-vercel-domain>
#   Redirect URLs: https://<your-vercel-domain>/**
# (include Preview deploy hosts too if you use Google/email redirects there)
#
# Migration: run supabase/migrations/0001_init.sql once in the hosted SQL
# Editor if the tables are not there yet. Do NOT run supabase/seed.sql on
# hosted Supabase — that seed is only for the local CLI stack.
